{{!-- One Tier's benefit list, in a Tier's own context.

	{{> "membership/benefits"}}

GUARDED, BECAUSE A TIER WITH NO BENEFITS IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL. Ghost auto-creates one paid tier
named after the site, with no description and no benefits at all, so a publication that has never
edited it would otherwise draw an empty bordered list in the middle of a price column. ADR 0003.

The caller owns the button below this list and has to take the auto margin when the list is gone:
`mb-auto` here is what pushes that button to the bottom of the column, so tiers.hbs writes
`{{#if benefits}}mt-[26px]{{else}}mt-auto{{/if}}` on it. The two are mutually exclusive on purpose —
both set `margin-top`, and which utility wins is decided by the compiled sheet rather than by the
order they appear in a class string.

Its own partial because the free column and the paid column draw the identical list, and the second
copy used to carry nothing but "guarded exactly as the free column above, and for the same
reason" — which is a comment admitting the duplication rather than removing it. --}}
{{#if benefits}}
	<ul class="mt-[22px] mb-auto flex list-none flex-col gap-[11px] p-0">
		{{#foreach benefits}}
			<li class="flex items-start gap-[11px]">
				<span
					aria-hidden="true"
					class="text-accent flex-none font-mono text-xs leading-[1.6]">&check;</span>
				<span class="text-small leading-[1.6]">{{this}}</span>
			</li>
		{{/foreach}}
	</ul>
{{/if}}
